{#
  How to Play, plus the definition paragraph under it. Verified structurally
  identical across word, draw and dance before extracting: same wrapper, same
  four numbered steps, and the only variation is whether a step body carries
  one paragraph or two. So `paras` is a list.

  The lobby's how-to modal clones this section's .howto-steps at runtime
  (word/app.js), so translating it here fixes the modal at the same time.

  `lead` is optional: a game with an illustration for this section supplies
  one, a game without simply omits the key. The alt text is the whole point
  of it. It is the only part of the picture a search engine or a model can
  read, so it states the rule rather than describing the drawing. The art and
  its geometry live in components/howto-lead.njk; only the words are here.
#}
{% from "components/howto-lead.njk" import howtoLead %}

{% macro howto(c, game="", id="how-to-play") %}
<section class="how-to-play" id="{{ id }}">
        <div class="howto-header">
          <h2>{{ c.heading | safe }}</h2>
          <p class="howto-sub">{{ c.sub | safe }}</p>
        </div>

{{ howtoLead(game, c.lead) }}
        <p class="howto-def">{{ c.def | safe }}</p>

        <ol class="howto-steps">
{% for step in c.steps %}
          <li class="howto-step">
            <div class="step-num">{{ loop.index }}</div>
            <div class="step-body">
              <h3>{{ step.h3 | safe }}</h3>
{% for p in step.paras %}
              <p>{{ p | safe }}</p>
{% endfor %}
            </div>
          </li>
{% endfor %}
        </ol>
{% endmacro %}
